  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Linquest has obligated $326M in federal contract money in FY2026 to date. Linquest won 46 awards so far, with an average award size of $7.1M. Obligations are down 12.5% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $171M, followed by the General Services Administration with $155M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the dominant market for Linquest, totaling $281M in obligations. All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services accounted for $24.1M and Engineering Services accounted for $20.7M. Historical fiscal-year totals show variability: FY21 was $223M, FY22 was $162M, FY23 was $318M, FY24 was $308M, FY25 was $372M, and FY26 is $326M. Current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing.",
    "sections": [
